0344-negroni-wlan-msi-mailbox: Wi-Fi, the chip's MSI into a RAM mailbox (boot-arg negroniwlan_msi, default 0 = no
change). Bit 0: at step 7 (after the PBL check, before BHI) the endpoint MSI capability (ID 5, bounded walk) gets the
IOVA of one word in our DMA pool (OFF_MSI 0x8000, its own 4 KiB page between the IPCR rings and the firmware) through
the negroniwlan_smmu=3 context, data base 0xa500, all vectors unmasked, MME = MMC, MSI enable. The word holds
0xffffffff; the BHI wait, every BOOT dump, the READY wait and the service pass print each change ("MSI #n data ..
(vector v) at <when> after N ms", at most 64 lines) and write the sentinel again. With MSI on, the event ring contexts
get msivec 1 and 2 (ath11k MHI irqs). No SMMU context, a mailbox outside the SMMU window or a 32-bit-only capability
with a high address: MSI stays off (one line, no stop). wlan_quiesce (every failure path) masks all vectors, clears
the enable bit, MME, address and data before the MHI reset, the frees and the SMMU teardown. Bit 1: PCIE_SOC_WAKE
(BAR0 0x3004) = 1 before BHI, 5 ms, readback logged (bisect only). The start line gets ", MSI N".

